From 01046659e4e67ac5761a136dc8eebc28cef9b4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:39:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add Google Cloud structured JSON output

Add -logformat=json-gcp with time, uppercase severity, message, and logging.googleapis.com/sourceLocation. Use the documented int64-string line number and map trace to DEBUG, since Cloud Logging has no TRACE severity. Keep category, thread and typed fields in the payload and reuse the generic JSON renderer without changing its schema.

Check keys against the official Cloud Logging/LogEntrySourceLocation specification. All 32 logging/event unit cases pass, and feature_logging exercises actual startup, mining, shutdown and file parsing for text, JSON, logfmt and GCP JSON. Cloud ingestion is specification-only: no cloud service or credentials were used. An accessor typo and the inherited structured caller-location defect found by these gates were repaired before committing.

(cherry picked from commit aba6c24788cc1b6e1baf8cf99158aa7496a22bcd)

